{"subject":"Microbiology","sourceTitle":"All In One Online","title":"PrepLadder · 7.Previous Year Questions","deckName":"created by tele @Neet_pg_bot::prep::Qbank::Microbiology::7.Previous_Year_Questions","questions":[{"id":"all-in-one-1760436526288","topic":"PrepLadder · 7.Previous Year Questions","number":1,"stem":"Choose the correct sterilization method for wire loop used in bacterial cultue.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Heat until the wire becomes red"},{"label":"B","text":"Autoclave"},{"label":"C","text":"Plasma sterilization"},{"label":"D","text":"Passing over flame × 3 times"}],"answer":"A","answerText":"Heat until the wire becomes red","solutionHtml":"<p>Wire loop is heated until the wire becomes red in colour, indicating sterilisation.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:NaN\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Sterilisation technique</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p><strong>Control method </strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>1. Hot air oven</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>c. <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"461ee544961692777182696a650b05\">Bacillus</span> atrophaeus/subtilis spores</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>2. Autoclave</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>d. <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"a1f8bd55901692777188b383607b48\">Geobacillus</span> stearothermophilus spores</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>3. <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"34cd707428169277719272942b7905\">Membrane</span> filtration</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>b. <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"6c0f4873b616927771989c0647cf3e\">Serratia</span> marcescens</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>4.Ionizing Radiation</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>a. <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"461ee544961692777182696a650b05\">Bacillus</span> pumilus</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p> </p>\n<p>These control methods are<strong> biological indicators </strong>used to check the <strong>effectiveness</strong> of the sterilisation method.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<ul>\n<li>Spores of <strong>bacillus atrophaeus/subtilis</strong> are used as a control method for hot air ovens and <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"8e2fdef08316927771877389af9cc7\">ethylene</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"e08c004e8f1692777194c9d37e17ad\">oxide</span> sterilisation (used mainly for heart-lung machines).</li>\n<li><strong>Spores of</strong><strong><em> </em></strong><strong>geobacillus stearothermophilus</strong> are used as a control method for <strong>autoclave</strong> and <strong>plasma sterilisation</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Bacillus globigi</strong> is also used as a control method for <strong>ethylene <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"e08c004e8f1692777194c9d37e17ad\">oxide</span> sterilisation</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Serratia marcescens</strong> and<strong><em> </em></strong><strong>Brevundimonas diminuta</strong> are used as control methods for <strong>membrane filters</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p> </p>\n<br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">1. Ananthanarayan and Paniker&rsquo;s Textbook of Microbiology, 10th Edition, Page 30-32.\n2. Essentials of Medical Microbiology- Apurba S Sastry and Sandhya Bhat, 3rd Edition, Page 22, 254-257.</div>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436526290","topic":"PrepLadder · 7.Previous Year Questions","number":2,"stem":"All of the following are cold sterilization methods except?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"UV rays"},{"label":"B","text":"Autoclave"},{"label":"C","text":"Gamma rays"},{"label":"D","text":"Plasma sterilisation"}],"answer":"B","answerText":"Autoclave","solutionHtml":"<p><strong>Autoclave is heat <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"f39be0f0871692777199459d86e0a7\">sterilization</span> of 121•*15min*15psi.</strong></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><img alt=\"\" data-author=\"NA\" data-hash=\"\" data-license=\"NA\" data-source=\"NA\" data-tags=\"\" height=\"4167\" src=\"images/exp_98_136_1.jpg\" width=\"2970\"/></p>\n<p> </p>\n<ul>\n<li>An <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"b4786b5c79169277718298b7590c38\">autoclave</span> is a sterilisation technique that uses moist heat at a temperature &amp;gt; 100<sup>o</sup>C.</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>The <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"b4786b5c79169277718298b7590c38\">autoclave</span> (steam steriliser) works on the principle of steam production under pressure.</li>\n<li>When this steam meets a cooler surface, it condenses, transferring its heat to that surface. The process continues until the surface temperature matches that of the steam.</li>\n<li>The resulting condensed water provides moist heat, effectively killing microbes on the materials by protein denaturation.</li>\n<li>Its temperature settings are 121<sup>o</sup>C for 15 minutes at 15 <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"536157be41169277719622efea0d20\">psi</span> pressure.</li>\n<li>Materials that can be sterilised include linen, <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"81d12f9cb01692777199e44ff3f3c1\">surgical</span> instruments(non-sharps only), laboratory ware, pharmaceuticals, <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"90dcd6e02316927771990a5c253ff7\">suture</span> material except catgut(cold sterilisation) and culture media except egg and <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"1ffaec13de169277719828374cfda0\">serum</span> containing media(inspissation).</li>\n<li>Sterilisation control indicator - <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"a1f8bd55901692777188b383607b48\">Geobacillus</span> stearothermophilus</li>\n</ul>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>Types of Autoclaves in Healthcare:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laboratory autoclaves</li>\n<li>Hospital <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"5d07a26d7516927771863e5f43d8d0\">dressing</span> sterilisers</li>\n<li>Instrument sterilisers</li>\n<li>Rapid <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"579dcf5fc51692777185eef17a83c6\">cooling</span> sterilisers</li>\n</ul>\n<br/><img src=\"images/exp_98_136_1.jpg\"/><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">1. Bailey & Scott&#39;s Diagnostic Microbiology, 15th Edition, Page 45-46\n2. Ananthanarayan and Paniker&rsquo;s Textbook of Microbiology, 10th Edition, Page 28-32</div>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436526292","topic":"PrepLadder · 7.Previous Year Questions","number":3,"stem":"Which test is used in the detection of long term glucose tolerance?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Fasting blood glucose"},{"label":"B","text":"Random blood glucose"},{"label":"C","text":"HbA1C"},{"label":"D","text":"CBC"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"HbA1C","solutionHtml":"p&amp;gt;\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>HbA1C</strong> (Glycated hemoglobin) is the test used to assess long-term <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"af3ae60c0c16927771889b84ca41c0\">glucose</span> tolerance and the average <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"88b48cf7241692777183e5f5b8adf1\">blood sugar</span> levels over the past 3 months. It reflects the percentage of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"ad2073fe6716927771885f3c1ec652\">hemoglobin</span> that has <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"af3ae60c0c16927771889b84ca41c0\">glucose</span> attached to it, providing an indicator of overall <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"88b48cf7241692777183e5f5b8adf1\">blood sugar</span> control.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Incorrect Options:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Fasting blood <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"af3ae60c0c16927771889b84ca41c0\">glucose</span> (Option A)</strong>: This measures <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"88b48cf7241692777183e5f5b8adf1\">blood sugar</span> levels after <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"67f123756d16927772026c46b8d27e\">fasting</span> for at least 8 hours. It is useful for diagnosing diabetes but does not provide a long-term view of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"af3ae60c0c16927771889b84ca41c0\">glucose</span> tolerance.</p>\n<p><strong>Random blood <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"af3ae60c0c16927771889b84ca41c0\">glucose</span> (Option B)</strong>: This measures blood <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"af3ae60c0c16927771889b84ca41c0\">glucose</span> at any time of the day, regardless of when the person last ate. It is useful for diagnosing diabetes, but again, it does not provide a long-term assessment.</p>\n<p><strong>CBC (Complete Blood Count) (Option D)</strong>: This is a blood test that measures various components of the blood, such as red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets. It is not related to <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"af3ae60c0c16927771889b84ca41c0\">glucose</span> metabolism.</p><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">The A1C Test & Diabetes - NIDDK</div>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436526294","topic":"PrepLadder · 7.Previous Year Questions","number":4,"stem":"Stain used to demonstrate fungal elements are?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Acid fast stain"},{"label":"B","text":"Gabbet's stain"},{"label":"C","text":"Methenamine silver"},{"label":"D","text":"Leifson & Ryu's stain"}],"answer":"C","answerText":"Methenamine silver","solutionHtml":"sed to <strong>demonstrate fungal elements</strong> in tissue samples. This <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"b29a1a16ab1692777199ede1c6e28b\">stain</span> binds to the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"97294d26a21692777184b7ddc59c4e\">cell wall</span> of <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"5ab0081e8316927772037e0f7c5a79\">fungi</span> and highlights the fungal structures, allowing them to be clearly visualized under the microscope. It is particularly useful in detecting fungal infections in tissues, as it stains the <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"5ab0081e8316927772037e0f7c5a79\">fungi</span> in a <strong>black</strong> color against a <strong>light background</strong>, making identification easier.\n\n<p><strong>Detection Methods for Fungi:</strong></p>\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Method</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Description</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Use</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Direct Microscopic Examination</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:middle\">\n<p><strong>KOH Preparation</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Dissolves <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d0e68b82ed1692777190fa10f7d4ba\">keratin</span> in clinical specimens (e.g., skin scrapings, nail clippings) to visualise fungal elements.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Diagnosing <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"84b9a43a7816927771867efa42a2dd\">dermatophyte</span> infections</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:middle\">\n<p><strong>Calcofluor White Staining</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Enhances fungal visibility by binding to <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"b24b4918a916927771844114519396\">chitin</span> in cell walls, causing them to fluoresce under UV light.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Observing fungal morphology</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:middle\">\n<p><strong>Gram Stain</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Traditionally for bacterial identification; also useful for yeasts, which typically <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"b29a1a16ab1692777199ede1c6e28b\">stain</span> Gram-positive (purple).</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Detecting certain fungi</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:middle\">\n<p><strong>India Ink Preparation</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Negative <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"3b007026bd16927771997ae809b603\">staining</span> method for <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"e26ba9a1d41692777187d0ad03a8c1\">encapsulated</span> yeasts (e.g., Cryptococcus neoformans), revealing a clear <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"95af91681416927771887742113c38\">halo</span> around cells.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Identifying <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"e26ba9a1d41692777187d0ad03a8c1\">encapsulated</span> yeasts</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:middle\">\n<p><strong>Methenamine Silver and <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"1e835060d3169277719499350aabe5\">PAS</span> Staining</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Histochemical techniques that <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"b29a1a16ab1692777199ede1c6e28b\">stain</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"5ab0081e8316927772037e0f7c5a79\">fungi</span> black (methenamine) or <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"9038419f6f169277719188195b72b5\">magenta</span> (PAS) in tissue sections.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Highlighting <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"5ab0081e8316927772037e0f7c5a79\">fungi</span> in tissues</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:middle\">\n<p><strong>Lactophenol Cotton Blue (LCB) Mount</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Enhances contrast in teased fungal colonies for <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"55beab619216927771925caac38373\">morphological</span> observation.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Microscopic examination of fungi</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Serology</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:middle\">\n<p><strong>Antibody Detection</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Identifies antibodies produced by the host in response to <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"5ab0081e8316927772037e0f7c5a79\">fungi</span> using methods like ELISA.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Tracking <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"dc6add5cf91692777189b30a6bae38\">immune response</span> to fungal infections</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:middle\">\n<p><strong>Antigen Detection</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Detects fungal antigens in body fluids using techniques such as <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"60088572d31692777191346a90b73f\">latex</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"36e1a07ab01692777180db73f01e84\">agglutination</span> tests.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Identifying fungal presence in the body</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Skin Tests</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:middle\">\n<p><strong>Delayed-Type Hypersensitivity (DTH)</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Assesses previous exposure to <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"5ab0081e8316927772037e0f7c5a79\">fungi</span> through localised reactions to <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"6a367ebd0c169277719091155a5b0f\">injected</span> antigens.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Evaluating past fungal exposure</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Newer Rapid Diagnostic Tests</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:middle\">\n<p><strong>Nucleic Acid Hybridisation</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Uses labelled DNA probes for rapid fungal DNA <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"723fdec66b1692777186e92f0c6fdf\">detection</span> in clinical samples.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Quick identification of fungal pathogens</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:middle\">\n<p><strong>Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR)</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Amplifies specific fungal DNA sequences, enabling early diagnosis even with low fungal loads.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #000000; border-left:1px solid #000000; border-right:1px solid #000000; border-top:1px solid #000000; vertical-align:top\">\n<p>Early <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"723fdec66b1692777186e92f0c6fdf\">detection</span> of fungal infections</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong>Acid fast <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"b29a1a16ab1692777199ede1c6e28b\">stain</span> (Option A)</strong>: This is used primarily for <strong>Mycobacterium species</strong> (e.g., <strong>Mycobacterium tuberculosis</strong>), not fungi. The <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"440f2b916316927771808b8ad44a64\">acid-fast</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"b29a1a16ab1692777199ede1c6e28b\">stain</span> highlights <strong>acid-fast bacilli</strong> by coloring them red, but it is not useful for fungal elements.</p>\n<p><strong>Gabbet's <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"b29a1a16ab1692777199ede1c6e28b\">stain</span> (Option B)</strong>: This is not a commonly used <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"b29a1a16ab1692777199ede1c6e28b\">stain</span> for fungi. It is a <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"0efdcdc9e01692777201003c81c85a\">variant</span> of Gram staining, primarily used for bacterial identification, not for fungi.</p>\n<p><strong>Leifson &amp; Ryu's <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"b29a1a16ab1692777199ede1c6e28b\">stain</span> (Option D)</strong>: This is a <strong>staining method for bacteria</strong>, especially to highlight <strong>flagella</strong> in bacterial samples, and it is not used to <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"b29a1a16ab1692777199ede1c6e28b\">stain</span> fungal elements.</p>\n<p> </p><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">Ananthanarayan & Paniker&rsquo;s Textbook of Microbiology, 6th Edition, Page 596, 597, 601</div>","tags":""},{"id":"all-in-one-1760436526296","topic":"PrepLadder · 7.Previous Year Questions","number":5,"stem":"Which one of the following is an enrichment medium?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Alkaline peptone water"},{"label":"B","text":"Monsur's taurocholate tellurite peptone water"},{"label":"C","text":"Selenite F broth"},{"label":"D","text":"All of the above"}],"answer":"D","answerText":"All of the above","solutionHtml":"rong&amp;gt;Enrichment Broth:\n<ul>\n<li>Liquid media with <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"1b6bd49bf11692777190214aa47f99\">inhibitory</span> agents selectively promote the growth of specific organisms and <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"6b3de87b7c16927771901326efbcd2\">inhibit</span> others.</li>\n<li>Used for isolating pathogens from clinical specimens containing normal <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"0af84af4761692777202fbf6914573\">flora</span> (e.g., stool, sputum).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Tetrathionate <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"46988d61a21692777183ac440c691a\">broth</span> – Used for <em>Salmonella Typhi</em> isolation.</li>\n<li>Gram-negative <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"46988d61a21692777183ac440c691a\">broth</span> – Used for <em>Shigella</em> isolation.</li>\n<li>Selenite F <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"46988d61a21692777183ac440c691a\">broth</span> – Used for <em>Shigella</em> isolation. <strong>(Option C)</strong></li>\n<li>Alkaline <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"34686cea521692777195ce0fbb7f69\">peptone</span> water (APW) – Used for <em>Vibrio cholerae</em> isolation. <strong>(Option A)</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Lim Broth</strong> is an <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"ba325c18481692777187ae8d082f45\">enrichment</span> <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"46988d61a21692777183ac440c691a\">broth</span> specifically used to enhance the growth of group B streptococci. It provides the necessary nutrients and conditions for the selective <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"ea15a8dedc1692777193399f05b191\">multiplication</span> of these organisms.</li>\n<li>Monsur's <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"d32711977216927772004e0d680631\">taurocholate</span> tellurite <span class=\"customMeta\" data-dictid=\"34686cea521692777195ce0fbb7f69\">peptone</span> water <strong>(Option B)</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<ol>\n</ol><br/><br/><div class=\"quiz-references\">Ananthanarayan and Paniker’s Textbook of Microbiology, 10th Edition, Page 39,40<br/>Mahon Lehman Textbook of Diagnostic Microbiology, 6th Edition, Page 114, 115, 974<br/>Apurba Sastry Essentials of Medical Microbiology, 3rd Edition Page 31</div>","tags":""}]}